  "//typesVersions": "Sprint 122 PR 4 (ADR-089) — typesVersions mirrors the exports map above, pointing at each subpath SOURCE file (enforced by src/__tests__/exportsTypesVersionsParity.test.ts). ts-jest forces moduleResolution:node10 whenever it forces module:commonjs — in EVERY 29.x — and node10 does not read exports maps, so without this every consumer test importing a @karmyq/shared subpath fails with TS2307. It points at SOURCE rather than dist deliberately: consumers on moduleResolution:node already resolved these subpaths to source, and CI type-checks them WITHOUT building shared, so a dist-pointing map breaks Lint & Type Check. Affects TYPE resolution only — Node still resolves exports to dist at runtime.",
